#
# This directory talks to two things the C++ Core Guidelines assume you are
# not talking to: a C ABI (the vendored display-list emitter) and a physical
# DDR region reached through mmap. Reinterpreting a mapped byte pointer as a
# volatile control word, casting away the volatile qualifier to hand a region
# to munmap, and walking pointers into a command ring are not smells here --
# they are the interface. Disabling them locally keeps the checks meaningful
# everywhere else rather than scattering NOLINT through every function.
#
# easily-swappable-parameters goes too: the signatures here are QPaintEngine's
# virtuals and the uio_rasterize_fn callback ABI, neither of which we get to
# reorder.
---
InheritParentConfig: true
Checks: >
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-reinterpret-cast,
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-const-cast,
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-pointer-arithmetic,
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-constant-array-index,
  -cppcoreguidelines-avoid-non-const-global-variables,
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-cstyle-cast,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
...
